=== DIAGNOSIS ===
The drift gate is doing its job and surfacing a real upstream defect that
landed in phase-42 prompt 0014 (commit aa46d37f8). The committed file
internal/tesla/protomodel/datum_decoder_gen.go does NOT match what
cmd/protogen-tesla/emit.go (committed in phase-42 prompt 0011, commit
8247353cd) currently emits.

Concretely, after running `go generate ./internal/tesla/protomodel/...`
the regenerated datum_decoder_gen.go diverges from the committed file
by 293 insertions / 243 deletions, including:

  Committed (0014):
    - declares ErrInvalid    = errors.New("protomodel: value marked invalid")
    - declares ErrUnsetValue = errors.New("protomodel: oneof value is unset")
    - imports github.com/teslamotors/fleet-telemetry/protos as ftproto
    - returns the typed compound structs from compounds.go
      (Doors, Time, TireLocation, Location)

  Generator (emit.go renderDatumDecoder, line 1124+):
    - declares ErrInvalidDatum = errors.New("protomodel: datum value is invalid")
      (different name, no unset-oneof sentinel)
    - REDEFINES Doors, Time, TireLocation INLINE in datum_decoder_gen.go,
      which collides with the same types declared in compounds.go and
      produces compile errors:
        datum_decoder_gen.go: Doors / Time / TireLocation redeclared in this block
        compounds.go: other declaration of Doors / Time / TireLocation
    - re-declares Datum / Payload / Value structs that compounds.go and
      datum_decoder_test.go do not expect

The test suite in internal/tesla/protomodel/datum_decoder_test.go was
also written against the committed shape (ErrInvalid, ErrUnsetValue,
compounds.go-typed Doors{...}), so accepting the generator's output as
the new canonical file would simultaneously break compilation AND
invalidate the test suite that was committed to lock the contract.

Resolution requires changes OUTSIDE prompt 0015's allowed file set
(prompt 0015 may only modify internal/tesla/protomodel/generate.go,
Makefile, .github/workflows/proto-gen-check.yml, and this log). One of:

  (a) reopen prompt 0014: update cmd/protogen-tesla/emit.go so
      renderDatumDecoder emits the ErrInvalid + ErrUnsetValue +
      compounds.go-aware shape that the committed file and tests
      already lock down; OR
  (b) issue a new corrective phase-42 prompt that re-aligns the
      generator (emit.go), the generated file, the test suite, and
      compounds.go in a single commit.

Per Honesty Covenant rules 1 (No red-as-green), 6 (No delegation /
no scope expansion), and 8 (No commit on red), this run is recorded
as BLOCKED. The drift gate itself works correctly -- it caught the
defect that prompt 0014 introduced. That is the intended behavior of
the gate this prompt was meant to wire up.

Side observation (not the cause of BLOCKED, informational only):
internal/tesla/protomodel/doc.go already carries a
`//go:generate go run ../../../cmd/protogen-tesla --proto ...
--out .` directive at line 23. The new generate.go directive added
by this prompt is intentionally the canonical anchor and matches the
prompt requirement, but its presence alongside doc.go's directive
means `go generate ./internal/tesla/protomodel/...` invokes the
binary twice (visible in === GO_GENERATE_DRY_RUN === above). The
generator is byte-stable per cmd/protogen-tesla TestEmitDeterministic,
so the duplicate run is harmless but wasteful; a future cleanup
prompt should remove the older directive from doc.go.

This is the same blocking condition reported by the previous attempt
at this prompt (commit 9767697b2). No upstream fix has landed since
that attempt, so the outcome is identical and equally BLOCKED. Only
this log file is committed; the new generate.go and
proto-gen-check.yml plus the Makefile gen-tesla / gen-tesla-check
targets remain uncommitted in the working tree so that the next
attempt can pick them up unchanged once the upstream emit.go vs
generated-file mismatch is resolved.

